{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"consequence-theorems","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:a6adce2af176e8100e5f874b46c0da40fde53f56940f925c820d53da0079f829/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7","passage_ref":"sha256:1fd49f692320db9f27935d8a5c8bc9bc22bddf38904cfd9fa8def31510d242d5/papers/long.md/sha256:a6adce2af176e8100e5f874b46c0da40fde53f56940f925c820d53da0079f829/papers/long.json/passages/consequence-theorems","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&paper=long&passage=consequence-theorems","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&paper=long&passage=consequence-theorems","span":{"end_byte":213512,"end_line":2401,"start_byte":190942,"start_line":2062},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&view=arguments&node=long.record-257bm-c19&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&node=long.record-257bm-c19&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&node=long.record-257bm-c19&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&view=arguments&node=long.record-257bm-c19&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&ref=sha256%3A72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696%2Fnodes%2Flong.record-257bm-c19","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c19"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c19"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c19","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.87 (An eventual nonnegative margin suffices)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.87, p. 69, label record:257bm-c19","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Fix a positive depth $k$ and put $D=G\\cap\\{2,\\ldots,k\\}$. The following conditions are equivalent:\n$$\nr_k(1/2)<2^{-(k+1)}\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n F_k(J)\\ge0\\ \\text{for some }J\\ge0.\n$$\nHere $F_k(J)$ is the integer expression defined in Theorem 6.13. Its normalised value is\n$$\n2^{-J}F_k(J)=\\sum_{i=1}^{J}c_D(k+1+i)2^{-i}-C_D(k).\n$$\nThis normalised expression, not necessarily $F_k(J)$ itself, is nondecreasing in $J$. Its limit is $1-2^{k+1}r_k(1/2)$, by the finite-support Lambert identity. This is positive exactly under the strict dyadic inequality on the left. At positive $k$, oddness of the reduced excess numerator excludes equality at zero.*\n\n*The result supplies some finite horizon, not the horizon $J=c-3$ required in the crossing application. More quantitatively, write $\\eta=1-2^{k+1}r_k(1/2)>0$. Since $\\sum_{r\\ge1}c_D(m+r)2^{-r}\\le m+2$, the omitted tail shows that $(k+J+3)2^{-J}<\\eta$ suffices for $F_k(J)>0$. The value $\\eta$ is rational for the finite support $D$, so this is an effective sufficient test. Proving it at the prescribed horizon is a separate arithmetic obligation.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257bm-c19","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257bm-c19","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c19%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_coeffTail_le_index_add_two%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"